                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "211d4d21-c631-3894-90e5-610375b8e022",
                        "entry_id": "256e391a-27f5-3c82-9c94-41bcebcad80c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "относящийся к Шанхаю, находящийся или созданный в Шанхае"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e04e67e6-a935-4d91-9c6f-caaf2428e1f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "256e391a-27f5-3c82-9c94-41bcebcad80c",
                        "source_sense_id": "211d4d21-c631-3894-90e5-610375b8e022",
                        "target_lang_word": "Shanghai",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Shanghai",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6220ff20-fd94-3e2b-98dc-167040f388a8",
                                        "entry_id": "624c60c9-97e6-3a52-a59b-42e1a525fd84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A major port city and direct-administered municipality of China, the largest urban area in China."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6044aabc-d45c-489f-8e2f-14681f42f195",
                                                "sense_id": "6220ff20-fd94-3e2b-98dc-167040f388a8",
                                                "text": "SHANGHAI (the emporium of Nanking) is the first town of any importance on the coast of Kiangnan province.[…]If, however, these difficulties were surmounted, and suitable precautions taken against existing dangers, the embouchure of this river would be one of the most eligible points for the establishment of British commerce in the whole empire. Be this as it may, however, certain it is that even now Shanghai carries on the greatest native trade of any port on the coast.[…]\nThe city of Shanghai is built on the left bank, some distance from the mouth. It is laid out with sufficient elegance, and numerous temples."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c65ed17c-0689-450e-ba28-41c41e6c98bb",
                                                "sense_id": "6220ff20-fd94-3e2b-98dc-167040f388a8",
                                                "text": "In January 1901, we reached Japan where Mrs. Hoover remained for the winter while I went to Shanghai in search of a method of reaching North China. The Port of Taku being frozen and there being then no railway connection between Shanghai and the north, all communication had been suspended for the winter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "563d13ea-1bca-4546-97a5-b9ab80d2bae5",
                                                "sense_id": "6220ff20-fd94-3e2b-98dc-167040f388a8",
                                                "text": "By the year 2000, Shanghai is scheduled to become an international center of commerce and finance; economic strategists predict that by 2010 the city will have become the world's largest trading center. This \"secret capital\" of China has set some ambitious goals for itself. The population is proudly celebrating their collective \"coming out,\" and business is booming."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "611d2021-53d2-467e-88eb-ce0db3769593",
                                                "sense_id": "6220ff20-fd94-3e2b-98dc-167040f388a8",
                                                "text": "Victor Li is determined to get married soon, but like many other young Chinese grappling with an uncertain economic outlook, the well-heeled Shanghai entrepreneur isn't sure he can afford to.\n\"It's very expensive for us to get married, especially in a big city like Shanghai,\" the 32-year-old said, as he took a break from a ticketed networking event for wealthier, top university-educated singles at an upmarket Shanghai jazz bar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05e6a09a-7052-344a-a896-7ce8aed8c6d9",
                                        "entry_id": "624c60c9-97e6-3a52-a59b-42e1a525fd84",
                                        "glosses": [
